Timeline
--------
1. Confirmed #32 by reading targets/node/deploy.sh: the only refusal is
   `rev-parse --verify` (the deadbee guard). No notion of a PR, window or
   berth. targets/bastille/deploy.sh has the same hole.
2. Read scenarios.org D9, which DEFERRED this fix on the grounds that a second
   window check inside every target is a second implementation of guard 3.
   That objection is correct and the design answers it: authorize.sh calls
   gates/preflight.sh rather than re-deriving anything, and is one script
   called by both targets. D9's own revisit trigger ("an agent driving
   deploy.sh unattended", "a workflow that calls a target directly") has
   fired twice over.
3. Verified gates/preflight.sh is read-only before delegating to it: no
   `gh pr edit`, no `gh pr comment`, no label writes. Safe to call from a
   deploy path.
4. MUTATION FOUND THREE VACUOUS ASSERTIONS. First run killed 7 of 10. P1 (node
   target stops calling the guard), P2 (jail target stops calling it) and P3
   (the call is piped) all SURVIVED -- the three most important mutations.
   Cause: C9/C9b grepped the RAW source for authorize.sh, and both targets
   carry comments naming authorize.sh and quoting `authorize.sh | sed` as the
   thing never to write. The greps matched the documentation and could not
   fail. Fixed by stripping comments before matching, and C9c added to assert
   the exit code is propagated. All three now die.
5. Verified against the LIVE forge, read-only:
     ./change/authorize.sh dev-3 <head>       -> exit 0, forge never asked
     ./change/authorize.sh staging 944c541    -> exit 1, heads no open PR
     ./change/authorize.sh staging 37d943b    -> exit 6 via preflight
   The last is PR #75: preflight judged the berth (#61 holds it) and the
   draft state, and the deploy path RECEIVED the refusal. That run also
   showed preflight returns 6, which this file's first header did not list --
   the contract is now an open-ended pass-through rather than a second copy
   of preflight's code table.
6. NOT RUN: neither deploy target was executed to completion or to refusal.
   The live estate is up and a bug would have touched staging's ports and
   deployment worktree. C9/C9b/C9c are static assertions and say so; P1/P2/P3
   confirm each can fail.

